TargaScript Method-Style Dot Notation
====================================

1. String Methods:
Original string: "  Hello, World!  "
After trim().upper(): "HELLO, WORLD!"

Original CSV string: apple,banana,cherry,date
After split(","): ["apple", "banana", "cherry", "date"]

Original sentence: The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog
After replace("fox", "cat"): The quick brown cat jumps over the lazy dog

Original complex string: "  mixed CASE string with EXTRA   spaces  "
After trim().lower(): "mixed case string with extra   spaces"

2. Array Methods:
Original array: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
After join("-"): 1-2-3-4-5
After map(double): [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]
After filter(even): [2, 4]
After reduce(sum, 0): 15

Odd numbers squared: [1, 9, 25]
Result of complex chaining: 24

3. Mixed Method Types:
Original array of strings: ["hello", "WORLD", "  TargaScript  "]
After processing and joining: "hello world targascript"

Original data string: NAME:John,AGE:30,CITY:New York
Processed data entries: [{"key": "name", "value": "John"}, {"key": "age", "value": "30"}, {"key": "city", "value": "New York"}]

Method-style dot notation examples completed!
